# fleet-warm-rust — per-repo Cargo dependency WARM image: pre-fetches ONE consuming repo's
# exact locked crates.io/git dependency set into the cargo registry cache baked into this
# image, so job-time `cargo build --offline` is a zero-egress cache hit instead of a fetch.
# COLD half of the cold/hot split (see docs/WORK_IMAGES.md "cold vs hot"): no application
# secret, no repo source checkout — only the two manifest files the consuming repo
# committed.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (not an optimization — required for correctness): same fact as
# Containerfile.warm-python — fleet runners have no general egress (measured 2026-07-26).
# `cargo fetch`/`cargo build` at job time inside a work container cannot reach
# crates.io/index.crates.io/a git dependency host at all. Baking the fetched registry+git
# cache at image-build time (on a builder that DOES have egress — the same assumption the
# rustup RUN steps in packaging/Containerfile already depend on; see
# .github/workflows/publish-images.yml's header for where that egress is expected to come
# from) is how the dependency set is ever present when the job actually runs.
#
# NO `rust` CLASS IMAGE EXISTS YET. packaging/image-map.example.toml says plainly: "Only
# base/shell/python are built today — rust/docs/gpu are not yet packaged." This file
# therefore CANNOT `FROM fleet-runner-rust:<semver>` the way Containerfile.warm-python FROMs
# fleet-runner-python — there is nothing to FROM. Rather than pretend that class exists,
# this file FROMs packaging/Containerfile's own output image (the pre-existing, un-classed
# "stock" image), which already carries a pinned rustup toolchain for UID 1001
# (RUST_TOOLCHAIN=1.96, CARGO_HOME=/home/runner/.cargo — see that file's header). This is a
# STATED, TEMPORARY DEPENDENCY on a stand-in, not a design claim that a rust class exists.
# Re-point the FROM at `fleet-runner-rust:<semver>` (built from a future
# Containerfile.runner-rust layered on fleet-runner-base, matching the shell/python
# pattern) once that class is packaged, and delete this note.
#
# TAG TENSION, flagged rather than papered over: this repo's style rule is
# "tag <name>:<semver>, NEVER :latest" (see packaging/Containerfile.runner-python etc.),
# but packaging/Containerfile — the image this file FROMs — has no semver tag defined
# anywhere in this repo; its only documented tag is `localhost/gha-runner-ctl:latest`
# (src/lib.rs DEFAULT_IMAGE, docs/WORK_IMAGES.md, docs/QUICKSTART.md all agree on this).
# Inventing a semver this repo does not actually use for that image would be worse than
# stating the gap, so BASE_TAG is an explicit ARG the builder must set to whatever tag of
# packaging/Containerfile it has locally; the default below matches what ships today.
# Update this default (and drop this paragraph) once packaging/Containerfile itself adopts
# semver tagging.
#
# BUILD CONTEXT CONTRACT: exactly the consuming repo's Cargo manifests, nothing else:
#   Cargo.toml
#   Cargo.lock   (required — the frozen, committed, reviewed resolution)
# Never the repo's source tree, never a secret (e.g. a private registry token or an SSH
# deploy key for a git dependency — those belong to the HOT path). Example:
#   mkdir -p /tmp/warm-ctx
#   cp Cargo.toml Cargo.lock /tmp/warm-ctx/
#   TAG="fleet-warm-rust:<repo>-$(sha256sum Cargo.lock | cut -c1-12)"
#   podman build -f packaging/Containerfile.warm-rust -t "$TAG" /tmp/warm-ctx
#
# SINGLE-PACKAGE ONLY, flagged gap: this file stubs out src/main.rs + src/lib.rs (below) so
# a bare Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock satisfies cargo's "must have a target" requirement without
# shipping the real source tree — the same trick cargo-chef/Docker Rust-caching recipes use.
# It does NOT handle a Cargo workspace with multiple member crates: `cargo fetch` on a
# workspace root manifest needs to see every member's own Cargo.toml (to walk path
# dependencies), and this file only copies the root manifest. A workspace repo would need
# its BUILD CONTEXT CONTRACT extended to include each member's Cargo.toml (stubbed the same
# way) — not implemented here; treat single-crate repos as the supported case for now.
#
# WHY `cargo fetch --locked` AND NOT plain `cargo fetch` / `cargo build`: `--locked`
# refuses to touch Cargo.lock — if Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock disagree (e.g. a version
# requirement moved since the lock was committed), the fetch fails loudly instead of
# silently re-resolving and baking a dependency set that disagrees with the lock the repo
# actually committed and reviewed. Same "generated artifact disagrees with its source"
# failure mode this fleet keeps hitting (see Containerfile.warm-python's header / PR #64's
# PyYAML story) — same fix: trust the committed lock or fail the build, never silently
# regenerate it.
#
# CONTENT ADDRESSING (provable cache hit / impossible-to-mistake-for-fresh staleness):
#   fleet-warm-rust:<repo>-<first 12 hex chars of `sha256sum Cargo.lock`>
# Recompute with:
#   sha256sum Cargo.lock | cut -c1-12
#
# Runs as non-root UID 1001 (inherited from packaging/Containerfile's `runner` user).
# Style: one logical step per RUN (no && chains).
#
# NO APPLICATION SECRET may appear in this file, its build ARGs, or its build context (a
# private crate registry token, an SSH key for a private git dependency). If a dependency
# needs one, that resolution step belongs in the HOT path at container instantiation, not
# baked here — say so rather than solving it with a secret in this file.
#
# COMPLEMENTARY CACHE (works today on podman 4.3.1, no Quadlet required — see
# docs/WORK_IMAGES.md "Quadlet" note): a named `podman volume` holding
# `$CARGO_HOME/registry` (e.g. `-v fleet-cargo-registry:/home/runner/.cargo/registry`) can
# additionally be mounted into warm-image builds and job containers to speed up repeat
# fetches across different repos/locks without depending on any baked layer. It is a
# complement to this image, not a substitute: it degrades gracefully but gives no
# content-addressed guarantee and no zero-egress guarantee on its own.

ARG BASE_TAG=latest
FROM localhost/gha-runner-ctl:${BASE_TAG}

USER runner
WORKDIR /home/runner/warm-src

# Manifests only — see header BUILD CONTEXT CONTRACT. Never the repo tree, never a secret.
COPY --chown=runner:runner Cargo.toml ./Cargo.toml
COPY --chown=runner:runner Cargo.lock ./Cargo.lock

# Stub source so cargo accepts the manifest without the real repo tree — see header
# SINGLE-PACKAGE ONLY note. Discarded content; exists only to satisfy cargo during fetch.
RUN mkdir -p src
RUN sh -c 'printf "fn main() {}\n" > src/main.rs'
RUN sh -c 'printf "" > src/lib.rs'

# --locked: never re-resolve — see header WHY. Fails the build (as intended) if Cargo.lock
# is missing or does not match Cargo.toml; a warm image with a silently-drifted lock is
# worse than no warm image at all. Populates $CARGO_HOME/registry and $CARGO_HOME/git.
RUN cargo fetch --locked
RUN cargo --version

WORKDIR /opt/actions-runner
